# {{app_title}}

A multi-page [Plotly Dash](https://dash.plotly.com) app using
[Dash Pages](https://dash.plotly.com/urls), scaffolded with
[dash-app](https://github.com/budescode/dash-app) on {{create_date}}.

## Run it

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
```

Or with [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (reads `pyproject.toml`):

```bash
uv sync
uv run app.py
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:8050 in your browser.

## Adding a page

Create a file in `pages/` and register it. That's the whole process:

```python
# pages/reports.py
import dash
from dash import html

dash.register_page(__name__, name="Reports")

layout = html.Div(html.H1("Reports"))
```

It appears in the navigation automatically at `/reports`.

## Project layout

| Path                 | Purpose                                               |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `app.py`             | App shell: navigation + `page_container`              |
| `pages/`             | One file per page, auto-routed by Dash Pages          |
| `assets/`            | CSS/JS files here are auto-loaded by Dash, no config |
| `requirements.txt`   | Python dependencies (pip)                             |
| `pyproject.toml`     | Same deps + metadata (uv, poetry)                     |

## Deploy

**Plotly Cloud**, the official hosting, free tier available:

```bash
pip install "dash[cloud]"
plotly user login
plotly app publish
```

The first publish creates a `plotly-cloud.toml` here; commit it, so future
publishes update the same app. Re-publish anytime with `plotly app publish`.

**Any WSGI host**: `app.py` exposes `server = app.server`:

```bash
pip install gunicorn
gunicorn app:server
```
